      {
        "ref": "1KI 1:18",
        "textualBasisJa": "Now, behold, Adonijah reigns; and you, my lord the king, don’t know it."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 1:24",
        "textualBasisJa": "Nathan said, “My lord, King, have you said, ‘Adonijah shall reign after me, and he shall sit on my throne’?"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 1:25",
        "textualBasisJa": "For he has gone down today, and has slain cattle, fatlings, and sheep in abundance, and has called all the king’s sons, the captains of the army, and Abiathar the priest. Behold, they are eating and drinking before him, and saying, ‘Long live King Adonijah!’"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 1:41",
        "textualBasisJa": "Adonijah and all the guests who were with him heard it as they had finished eating. When Joab heard the sound of the trumpet, he said, “Why is this noise of the city being in an uproar?”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 1:42",
        "textualBasisJa": "While he yet spoke, behold, Jonathan the son of Abiathar the priest came; and Adonijah said, “Come in; for you are a worthy man, and bring good news.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 1:43",
        "textualBasisJa": "Jonathan answered Adonijah, “Most certainly our lord King David has made Solomon king."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 1:49",
        "textualBasisJa": "All the guests of Adonijah were afraid, and rose up, and each man went his way."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 1:50",
        "textualBasisJa": "Adonijah was afraid because of Solomon; and he arose, and went, and hung onto the horns of the altar."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 1:51",
        "textualBasisJa": "Solomon was told, “Behold, Adonijah fears King Solomon; for, behold, he is hanging onto the horns of the altar, saying, ‘Let King Solomon swear to me first that he will not kill his servant with the sword.’”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 2:13",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then Adonijah the son of Haggith came to Bathsheba the mother of Solomon. She said, “Do you come peaceably?” He said, “Peaceably."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 2:19",
        "textualBasisJa": "Bathsheba therefore went to King Solomon, to speak to him for Adonijah. The king rose up to meet her and bowed himself to her, and sat down on his throne and caused a throne to be set for the king’s mother; and she sat on his right hand."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 2:21",
        "textualBasisJa": "She said, “Let Abishag the Shunammite be given to Adonijah your brother as wife.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 2:22",
        "textualBasisJa": "King Solomon answered his mother, “Why do you ask Abishag the Shunammite for Adonijah? Ask for him the kingdom also, for he is my elder brother; even for him, and for Abiathar the priest, and for Joab the son of Zeruiah.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 2:23",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then King Solomon swore by the LORD, saying, “God do so to me, and more also, if Adonijah has not spoken this word against his own life."
